(Operating Systems - Unit 3: Deadlocks) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A deadlock is a situation where a set of processes are blocked,) Tj T*
(because each process is holding a resource and waiting for) Tj T*
(another resource held by some other process.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Four necessary conditions \(Coffman conditions\):) Tj T*
(1. Mutual exclusion: a resource can be used by only one process.) Tj T*
(2. Hold and wait: a process holds one resource and waits for more.) Tj T*
(3. No preemption: a resource cannot be taken away by force.) Tj T*
(4. Circular wait: processes wait for each other in a cycle.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
