stream
BT /F1 14 Tf 60 780 Td 18 TL
(Handling deadlocks) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Prevention: make sure at least one condition can never hold.) Tj T*
(Avoidance: grant a request only if the system stays in a safe state.) Tj T*
(The Banker's algorithm is the classic avoidance algorithm.) Tj T*
(Detection and recovery: allow deadlocks, detect them with a) Tj T*
(wait-for graph, then recover by killing or rolling back a process.) Tj T*
(Ignoring: many operating systems simply ignore the problem) Tj T*
(\(the ostrich algorithm\) because deadlocks are rare.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
